    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on **Corbin Carroll** and **Seiya Suzuki** tonight, our two premier options with efficiency scores of 84.82 and 73.90, respectively. **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime position against Canning, benefiting from a +19% boost due to the starter's poor xERA and an ideal order placement in the three-hole. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** capitalizes on a high-ceiling park factor (+16%) and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Rogers, making him an elite play. While **Kyle Karros** occupies a lower tier, his score of 63.93 is bolstered significantly by a +5% wind-out factor and a +7% platoon advantage, proving that the algorithm is aggressive on favorable atmospheric conditions when the opposing arm, Whisenhunt, is struggling to limit contact.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jose Caballero**, who narrowly missed the starting threshold with a score of 39.32. While we are perpetually hunting for his speed, the combination of Rasmussen\u2019s sharper skill set and a poor platoon fit rendered him a \"Below Floor\" risk; preserving a game cap for a better matchup is the more disciplined choice for our 5x5 push. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** remains a locked-in start at 63.01 despite the 38% rain risk. The calculation accounts for his aggressive base-running against a slow-delivering Pallante, providing enough stolen base upside to outweigh the weather volatility. Elsewhere, **Cole Young** sits at a marginal 47.41; he remains in the lineup due to lack of superior alternatives, though his -3% platoon hit against Junk highlights the narrow margin he currently occupies in our daily plans.",
